Two parts of the request are not in this crate. The node's world imports only `aap:caps/state-read`, and the target has no WASI. It therefore has no file-system access, so it cannot append to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`. It also has no `http-client` import, so it cannot call the metadata service. Adding either would mean granting the node authority its contract doesn't include. I left both out, and the output is unchanged. If you want them, the log line should come from the host that runs the node, and the enrichment should be a separate node holding `http-client` with that host allowlisted.

The node reads the `urls` key from the `subscriptions` store, which holds newline-separated URLs. It trims each line and drops blank ones. A missing key gives an empty list.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = state_read::get("urls")
            .map(|raw| {
                raw.lines()
                    .map(|l| l.trim())
                    .filter(|l| !l.is_empty())
                    .map(|l| l.to_string())
                    .collect::<Vec<String>>()
            })
            .unwrap_or_default();
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
